tituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}310 & =2({2}^{7})+3({2}^{4})+C \\\\ 310 & =304+C \\\\ C & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=2{t}^{7}+3{t}^{4}+6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba3e3eeedee886545a79a71018c23daf2987e2a1f746029771da26d1bea2b3f6"} {"question" "q-350978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2f8408a328e5b806c1e628bc71ca6c654340d1174eadb0a141f5e98abbefdb"} {"question" "q-350978" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba3e3eeedee886545a79a71018c23daf2987e2a1f746029771da26d1bea2b3f6"} {"question" "q-350978" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t^7+3t^4+6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba3e3eeedee886545a79a71018c23daf2987e2a1f746029771da26d1bea2b3f6"} {"question" "q-351004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=100\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba3e3eeedee886545a79a71018c23daf2987e2a1f746029771da26d1bea2b3f6"} {"question" "q-351004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{5}+2{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=100.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100 & =3({2}^{5})+2({2}^{3})+C \\\\ 100 & =96+16+C \\\\ 100 & =112+C \\\\ C & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{t}^{5}+2{t}^{3}-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba3e3eeedee886545a79a71018c23daf2987e2a1f746029771da26d1bea2b3f6"} {"question" "q-351004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2f8408a328e5b806c1e628bc71ca6c654340d1174eadb0a141f5e98abbefdb"} {"question" "q-351004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba3e3eeedee886545a79a71018c23daf2987e2a1f746029771da26d1bea2b3f6"} {"question" "q-351004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3t^5+2t^3-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063982/state.json" "file